 "drivingQuestion": "What counts as 'lacking trapping'?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Shmuel's definition given (challenged in the next unit)",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "beitzah.24a.12",
   "daf": "24a",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "זֶה הַכְּלָל כׇּל הַמְחוּסָּר צֵידָה וְכוּ׳. הֵיכִי דָּמֵי מְחוּסָּר צֵידָה? אָמַר רַב יוֹסֵף אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: כׇּל שֶׁאוֹמֵר הָבֵא מְצוּדָה וּנְצוּדֶנּוּ.",
   "en": "It was further taught in the mishna: «This is the principle: Any» animal inside such an enclosure «whose trapping is inadequate» may not be caught and removed from there on a Festival, whereas any animal whose trapping is not inadequate may be apprehended and removed from there. The Gemara asks: «What are the circumstances» of an animal «whose trapping is inadequate? Rav Yosef said» that «Rav Yehuda said» that «Shmuel said: Any» animal «with regard to which one would say: Bring a trap so that we may catch it,» as the animal cannot be apprehended without the aid of a trap."
  }
 ],
